# playpick cell: mode=walk boss=marrow spec=hunter:marksmanship style=flee
# size=10 difficulty=normal view=1280x800 save=fresh. 10-normal is
# progress.ts's first rung, open on a fresh save with no unlock trick
# needed, so this walks in cold with no invite-hash recipe. boss=marrow is
# a coverage label only -- `evening` steers at no boss (direction.md's own
# repeated note under [[#6]]) -- so this walks in at the door same as any
# other.
#
# What is actually new here: [[#6]] (THE VIGIL stalls one evening in five
# regardless of style) has been narrowing toward "a class's own flat
# moveSpeed decides whether the corridor is a wall," on the strength of
# rogue:assassination (moveSpeed 178, highest in the roster) crossing clean
# three-for-three where warrior/paladin/priest/warlock/druid/shaman/mage
# (moveSpeed 158-167) have stalled more often than not at 10-normal. No
# session has yet tried the *second*-fastest class -- hunter, at 173,
# `src/sim/classes.ts` -- against this exact stall. flee had already stalled
# once at 10-normal on a slower class (priest:discipline, 2026-09-25) and
# crossed clean twice at 25-heroic (shaman:restoration, hunter:marksmanship
# itself in a different session) -- so this is also the first test of
# whether a fast class crosses 10-normal clean under a style that has
# already stalled once at that exact size/difficulty under a different
# class.
open
targets
shot front
tap raid
shot raid-setup
tap next
tap class:hunter:marksmanship
shot class-selected
tap pull
waitscreen fight 15
state
shot arrive-threshold

evening flee 300 6
state
bill
shot end
